/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  constant/economics -- the prices this appraisal is priced at.  Currency:
  EUR per kg of the stream named.

  THE TWO PRICES THAT DECIDE THE APPRAISAL come from the design-basis
  dossier (docs/design/apalutamide-design-basis-dossier.md); every other price is an AUTHOR-SET ASSUMPTION, a round
  figure chosen so that the appraisal can run, NOT market data -- a group
  replaces each with a dated, cited figure before quoting an NPV.  The
  provenance block of each says which, in the words the engine carries to
  its output.

    * the TABLET, SOLD: 4.0 EUR per 60 mg tablet, NET EX-FACTORY.  The
      business case is a GENERIC ENTRANT AT LOSS OF EXCLUSIVITY (Vitor's
      ruling, DEV.md 4c C99 addendum: a price with 2-4 competitors).  The
      dossier (section 4.4) takes the originator's German ex-factory price,
      about 19.13 EUR per tablet (back-calculated from the pharmacy price
      with the statutory margins, AMPreisV), and the FDA's median generic
      price cut at 4 competitors, 79 % (Conrad & Lutter, FDA 2019): about
      4.0 EUR.  At 2 competitors (a 54 % cut) it is about 8.8 EUR -- the
      other end of the ruling, run as an economic sensitivity in
      system/postDict.  US data applied to Europe: an estimate.  The stream
      `packagedTablets` carries 11.2219 kg/h for 15 468.75 tablets/h
      (0.72546 g a tablet: the 700 mg core, the 21 mg coat and the
      water the coat keeps), so the price per kg of that stream is
      4.0 / 0.00072546 = 5513.8 EUR/kg.  If the formulation, the coat or
      the reject fraction moves, so does the tablet mass: redo this division
      (it does not follow the run).
    * the API, BOUGHT: 7 776 EUR/kg of apalutamide, the only public signal
      (dossier section 3.5): Pharmaoffer's average recorded price, 8 452 USD/kg
      over the 12 months to 31 May 2026, x 0.92 (the case's usdToEur).  It is
      an average of small pre-generic lots; a tonne-scale contract price was
      NOT found -- ask two or three DMF holders for a dated quotation.  The
      60 mg in a tablet then costs 0.47 EUR.

  THE RECOVERED ACETONE IS NOT SOLD (dossier section 5, item 11): a GMP plant
  reuses its recovered solvent in-process after validation (a raw-material
  credit, which this base case does not take -- it does not close the loop)
  or sends it to licensed recovery or incineration, usually at a cost.  Its
  disposal cost was NOT found (a waste contractor's quotation), so it is NOT
  in the operating cost either: the appraisal is optimistic by that amount.

  NOT PRICED: the recovered acetone (above), the purge gas (to vent
  treatment, not modelled), the coating
  exhaust (to atmosphere through a filter, not modelled) and the rejected
  tablets (their disposal is a cost the plant does not carry here).
  The UTILITIES (steam, cooling water, ammonia refrigeration, the blower's
  electricity) are priced from their records by the utility allocation.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
products
(
    {
        stream    packagedTablets;
        price     5513.8;             // EUR/kg = 4.0 EUR/tablet, see header
        costYear  2026;
        provenance
        {
            origin  "docs/design/apalutamide-design-basis-dossier.md section 4.4 (derived from estimates): a generic at loss of exclusivity with 4 competitors, the originator's German ex-factory price (about 19.13 EUR/tablet, section 3.2) less the FDA's 79 % median cut (Conrad & Lutter, FDA 2019, section 3.4)";
            method  "4.0 EUR per 60 mg tablet, NET EX-FACTORY, divided by the run's tablet mass (header); the 2-competitor end, 8.8 EUR, is the economic sensitivity in system/postDict";
        }
    }
);
